WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.545
The Canadian Forces Aptitude Test was eliminated in October 2024.

00:00:04.545 --> 00:00:10.204
Replaced by the Scored Employment Application Form — a biography-based assessment with no cognitive floor.

00:00:10.204 --> 00:00:16.886
The IQ-based screening that defined Canadian military recruitment for decades was removed by General Jennie Carignan's directive.

00:00:16.886 --> 00:00:22.920
The Canadian Armed Forces are sixteen thousand personnel short of authorized strength as of 2023.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:28.238
Training capacity is capped at six thousand four hundred recruits per year through basic training.

00:00:28.238 --> 00:00:35.090
The missing middle problem — experienced mid-career personnel leaving faster than they can be replaced — is driving the collapse.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:41.329
With the cognitive floor removed, bottom-quartile recruitment is now structurally possible through experiential grading.

00:00:41.329 --> 00:00:43.420
This is not a recruitment crisis.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:46.704
This is a capability crisis engineered through policy.
